From 8dd28ef8d002b4f49c38ba605eb2f25e4a2d8554 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 20:45:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: keep perfmon enabled so kernel devfreq sees
 GPU load

The a2xx kernel devfreq driver reads the RBBM busy perfcounter to estimate
GPU load for DVFS. That counter only advances while the perfmon is enabled
via CP_PERFMON_CNTL, which fd2_emit_restore programs every batch. The stock
code emitted COND(FD_DBG(PERFC), 1) -- i.e. 0 unless the perfc debug flag was
set -- so during normal rendering the perfmon was frozen every batch, the
busy counter never moved, devfreq saw ~0 load and parked the GPU at its
minimum OPP (no upward clock scaling). Emit 1 unconditionally so the counter
runs and the governor can scale the GPU clock with load.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
index da5c99188e7..74e5ea312cb 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
@@ -417,7 +417,14 @@ fd2_emit_restore(struct fd_context *ctx, struct fd_ringbuffer *ring)
 
    /* enable perfcntrs */
    OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_CP_PERFMON_CNTL, 1);
-   OUT_RING(ring, COND(FD_DBG(PERFC), 1));
+   /*
+    * Keep the perfmon enabled unconditionally (not only under FD_DBG(PERFC)):
+    * the a2xx kernel devfreq driver reads the RBBM busy perfcounter to gauge
+    * GPU load, and that counter only advances while the perfmon is enabled.
+    * The old COND default emitted 0 every batch, freezing the counter, so
+    * devfreq saw ~0 load and parked the GPU at its minimum OPP (no scaling).
+    */
+   OUT_RING(ring, 1);
 
    /* note: perfcntrs don't work without the PM_OVERRIDE bit */
    OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_RBBM_PM_OVERRIDE1, 2);
-- 
